From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:09:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Blu-ray 3D: forget a 3D playlist's extension at the next
 playlist

The 3D flags were set when a playlist has an MVC extension and never
cleared, so a menu moving from a 3D playlist to a 2D one went on opening
an extension, with a play item the 2D playlist's sub-path does not have.
They are now cleared for each playlist, and also when the extension is
disabled, and the open checks the sub-path and the play item. Disabling
the extension clears the flag that keeps the clip start of a 3D playlist
unheld, so a 3D playlist played in 2D holds it as a 2D one does.

An open that failed before the file kept the 3D flag set with no
extension demuxer, which the stream setup then used. It clears the flag,
and the stream setup and the pairing now check that the demuxer exists.

Shared code, unavoidable: the 3D Blu-ray demuxer exists only in
CoreELEC's Kodi (DVDInputStreamBluray, CDemuxMVC, CDemuxStreamSSIF and
their use in DVDDemuxFFmpeg) and has no AML counterpart.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp           | 2 +-
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp          | 3 +++
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index 57fe8341..ff3d3574 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -2448,7 +2448,7 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
             AVStream *mvcStream = nullptr;
             const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream> pExt = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDVDInputStream::IExtentionStream>(m_pInput);
 
-            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention())
+            if (pExt && pExt->HasExtention() && pExt->GetExtentionDemux())
             {
               delete m_pSSIF;
               m_pSSIF = new CDemuxStreamSSIF();
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
index da8de522..5cf495a6 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DemuxStreamSSIF.cpp
@@ -199,6 +199,9 @@ bool CDemuxStreamSSIF::FillMVCQueue(double dtsBase)
     return false;
 
   CDemuxMVC* demux = m_bluRay->GetExtentionDemux();
+  if (!demux)
+    return false;
+
   DemuxPacket* mvc;
   while ((m_MVCqueue.size() < MVC_QUEUE_SIZE) && (mvc = demux->Read()))
   {
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
index e591af33..6e456117 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp
@@ -758,6 +758,7 @@ void CDVDInputStreamBluray::DisableExtention()
   CloseMVCDemux();
   m_bMVCDisabled = true;
   m_bMVCPlayback = false;
+  m_hasMVCExtension = false;
 }
 
 int CDVDInputStreamBluray::Read(uint8_t* buf, int buf_size)
@@ -1583,6 +1584,8 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::ProcessItem(int playitem)
 
   m_titleInfo = bd_get_playlist_info(m_bd, playitem, m_angle);
 
+  m_bMVCPlayback = false;
+  m_hasMVCExtension = false;
   if (!m_bMVCDisabled)
   {
     MPLS_PL * mpls = bd_get_title_mpls(m_bd);
@@ -1658,8 +1661,12 @@ bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::OpenNextStream()
 bool CDVDInputStreamBluray::OpenMVCDemux(int playItem)
 {
   MPLS_PL *pl = bd_get_title_mpls(m_bd);
-  if (!pl)
+  if (!pl || !ClipAt(playItem) || m_nMVCSubPathIndex >= pl->ext_sub_count ||
+      playItem >= pl->ext_sub_path[m_nMVCSubPathIndex].sub_playitem_count)
+  {
+    m_bMVCPlayback = false;
     return false;
+  }
 
   std::string strFileName;
   strFileName.append(m_root);
